ngspice in KaCad 8

Comparison of four bit full adders,
a ripple carry, made of NAND gates,
with the 74HC283.

Input with a home made symbol (HV_test.kicad_sym) and ngspice model (DS9b.lib),
using the d_source code model and the stimulus input file fuadd4.stim.

74xxx model files are 74HC00m.lib and 74HC283m.lib.

Data are stored in a vcd file.

Plotting uses gtkwave (plotting with Eeschema is not (yet) possible),
a tcl script (nggtk.tcl) is called to read and parse the data in gtkwave.

The whole procedure is controlled by a ngspice .control script.

Simulation time on an i9 is a mere 9ms.

To run the simulation, the .control scipt on the Eeschema canvas has to be edited:
Fill in your project path, where the model and other input files are stored.

When exported into a ngspice netlist (FullAddComp.cir), standard ngspice may be
used as well to run the simulation.

The disadvantages of the ripple carry adder are obvious: it is slower, it has
glitches in the output data.
